; ── R + ASSOCIATIVITY as ORIENTED rules: the A-vs-B clash ──
; Adding cmp-assoc as a directed rule.  Claim: TERMINATING but NOT CONFLUENT.
; Critical pair on  cmp(cmp(os(x),os(y)),z) :
;     os/os  ⇒  cmp(os(cmp(x,y)), z)
;     assoc  ⇒  cmp(os(x), cmp(os(y), z))
; — no common reduct (for variable z), so confluence FAILS.  This is exactly the
; obstruction we hit:  elimination and associativity cannot be ORIENTED together.
(VAR x y z)
(RULES
  cmp(x,od(y))     -> od(cmp(x,y))
  cmp(os(x),os(y)) -> os(cmp(x,y))
  cmp(od(x),os(y)) -> od(cmp(x,y))
  cmp(oz,oz)       -> oz
  cmp(cmp(x,y),z)  -> cmp(x,cmp(y,z))
)
